# Assignment 1 – Grabify IP Logger Awareness

## Description

Grabify is an IP logging tool used to demonstrate how clicking on a specially generated URL can reveal publicly available network information such as the visitor's IP address and browser details. This exercise was conducted only for cybersecurity awareness in an isolated lab environment.

---

## Procedure

1. Open the Grabify website.
2. Enter a test URL.
3. Generate a tracking link.
4. Open the generated link using a test device or virtual machine.
5. Observe the information collected in the Grabify dashboard.

---

## Information Observed

- Public IP Address
- Date and Time
- Browser Information
- Operating System
- Device Type
- Country (Approximate)
- User Agent
- Referring URL (if available)

---

## Learning Outcome

- Understood how IP logging works.
- Learned how attackers may collect publicly available information through phishing links.
- Recognized the importance of verifying links before clicking them.

